  "notes": "Official Clemson Biosystems Engineering '2021-2022 Curriculum' (Department of Environmental Engineering and Earth Sciences), 130 Total Semester Hours. Two senior-year emphases are published; this seed is the Ecological Engineering Emphasis. Freshman year is the General Engineering core. Sophomore semester split (18/18) follows the published semester totals: ENGR 2100 in first semester, ENGL 3140, MICR 3050/3501 and Global Sustainability in second. Junior year is common to both emphases. Ecological Requirement = BIOL, FOR, HORT, MICR, PES or WFB 3000-level or above; Ecological Engineering Requirement = BE, CE or EES 3000-level or above. FOR 4340 GIS is recommended and may count as either the Global Sustainability option or the Ecological option. A 2.0 engineering GPA is required for graduation. Per-course prerequisites are in the Clemson Undergraduate Catalog; prereq arrays left empty.",
